  "summary": "Record independent authorization verdict expectations and the remaining shared Python control boundary.",
  "why": "Luis moved Shop work to another task and approved the bounded Core authorization comparison. Inspection found no production defect, but both paths share the same verdict calculator. Add a literal nine-case neutral answer table and 30 tests for order, typed refusal, immutability and deliberately wrong shared rules. Correct the earlier independent-recipe wording and record the finite profile's deliberate restrictions. The focused selection passes 123 tests; the separate existing protocol and authorization-history suites pass 251 tests. Ruff and formatting pass. This is test strengthening, not production RED/GREEN, a full repository gate, a second interpreter, a public policy artifact or an Assent cutover. No runtime, ontology, package, Shop, paper or downstream consumer changes. The existing replacement backlog remains open; extracting identified control semantics is a next design cut, not silently activated by this entry.",
